1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Welcome to the technical overview of Stock-AI: a quantitative machine learning research platform.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Financial markets represent one of the lowest signal-to-noise ratio domains in applied artificial intelligence.

3
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:22,000
While academic literature frequently reports inflated directional forecasting accuracies, they often collapse out-of-sample.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:30,000
Our goal is to establish an academically rigorous, leakage-free benchmark across equities with zero lookahead bias.

5
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:42,000
We systematically evaluate whether fusing financial news sentiment with price series yields genuine predictive alpha.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Our research builds upon recent work published in Neural Computing and Applications (DOI: 10.1007/s00521-024-10303-1).

7
00:00:54,500 --> 00:01:03,000
The target is binary classification: forecasting whether the Close price on day t exceeds the Close price on day t-1.

8
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:13,000
The market branch processes a 20-day by 16-feature temporal tensor through stacked Bidirectional LSTMs.

9
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:23,000
The linguistic branch extracts dense 768-dimensional FinBERT embeddings from financial news headlines.

10
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:34,000
Both representations project into a common 64-dimensional latent subspace for downstream multimodal fusion.

11
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Absolute data integrity is non-negotiable. We eliminate data leakage through three strict architectural guarantees.

12
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:18,000
First: Strict Chronological Partitioning. Training through 2022, validation through mid-2024, and 6,292 test sessions.

13
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:27,500
Second: Sequence Isolation. Every 20-day market window strictly terminates on trading session t-1.

14
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:37,000
MinMax scaling parameters are fit solely on training data, preventing cross-temporal distributional leakage.

15
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:49,000
Third: Transparent Provenance. For delisted ATVI, 12-ticker validation is marked BLOCKED due to unverified legacy data.

16
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:58,000
All modern forward-testing benchmarks are strictly evaluated across the eleven validated active equities.

17
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:39,000
We explore multiple tiers of model complexity: heuristics, linear models, and recurrent neural networks.

18
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:48,000
Our baselines include Training-Majority, Direction Persistence, and Logistic Regression on t-1 features.

19
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:57,000
For multimodal fusion, we implement a Gated Multimodal Unit (GMU) rather than naive feature concatenation.

20
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:07,000
The GMU learns a gating vector z to perform a convex combination between market sequences and news embeddings.

21
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:18,000
This dynamically suppresses linguistic noise during calm periods while elevating sentiment during corporate catalysts.

22
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Evaluating across 6,292 out-of-sample forward test observations reveals crucial financial realities.

23
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:35,000
The Majority baseline achieves 52.13% accuracy simply by aligning with upward market drift during 2024 to 2026.

24
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:44,500
The BiLSTM ensemble achieves 51.30% accuracy while making balanced predictions across both bull and bear sessions.

25
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:54,500
Direction Persistence achieves the highest Macro F1 at 0.4953, while Logistic Regression achieves 0.4930.

26
00:05:55,000 --> 00:06:05,000
In modern efficient equity markets, directional edge is modest and does not constitute an automated trading arbitrage.

27
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:15,000
All claims of sixty-five to seventy-five percent directional forecasting are artifacts of future leakage.

28
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:10,000
Stock-AI is packaged as a complete research platform with core library, REST API, and dashboard.

29
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:19,500
The Python library features data downloaders, technical indicators, window builders, and 51 passing tests.

30
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:29,000
FastAPI exposes endpoints for ticker metadata, historical OHLCV series, technical indicators, and inference.

31
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:39,000
The React/TypeScript frontend provides an interactive Stock Explorer, Model Lab, and Prediction Demonstration.

32
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:50,000
Explicit disclaimers clarify that all model outputs are academic research benchmarks, not financial advice.

33
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:40,000
Daily news headlines lack intraday timestamps, warranting a conservative TIMING-LIMITED designation.

34
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:50,000
Future research will integrate high-frequency SEC Edgar 8-K filings and cross-asset graph attention networks.

35
00:08:50,500 --> 00:09:00,000
The complete codebase, reproduction scripts, and verified benchmark artifacts are open source on GitHub.

36
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:12,000
Visit github.com/Kavix28/Stock-AI for documentation, reproduction steps, and full benchmark records.

37
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:25,000
Thank you for exploring Stock-AI: advancing quantitative rigor and intellectual honesty in financial AI.
